<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Drasco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 809</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Thrasco, Drożko</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Drasco was a prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obotrites">Obotrites</a>, a West Slavic people of present-day Mecklenburg and eastern Holstein, and an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>. In 798 he led the Obotrites to victory over the Nordalbingian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> near Bornhöved. After the Danish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gudfred">Gudfred</a> attacked his lands in 808 he had to give hostages to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a>, and he was murdered in 809.</p></div>
